endored file and the bots, and lists no Dana share as a major owner. Dana has no stated line count, but nothing credits her with a large share.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Priya has 28 lines (1.4%), the re-applied lines stay with Priya, and Tomás is credited with 13 lines even though Hartley committed them. Tomás's count is close to the truth of 15, and the explicit credit-correction note supports the pass.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"It states the bus factor is 1 now (Hartley alone). The top two hold 66.4% of non-blank lines, which is in range.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"It names Smith and Delgan as inactive. It gives 44.1% of lines belonging to people with no commit in the window, which is outside 25-35%. It also treats Yaari as having had no commit since 2022, which is wrong, and that error inflates the departed share.\", \"pass\": false}], \"D\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Hartley is 56% and Yaari 12%, with Yaari second. It deliberately did not merge the wiggin15 identity, but it reports 232 lines, which matches the truth.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"It excludes the vendored file and the quote reformat. Dana appears only as a handful of lines, and no bot gets lines.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Priya's cursor helpers are not credited, and the answer says nothing about the reapply. Tomás's patch is not mentioned.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"It says the top two hold about 68%, which is in range. It never states the bus factor, and it does not say that Hartley alone holds more than half.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"It gives no departed-lines share, and it does not say Smith and Delgan are gone. It says it hasn't checked.\", \"pass\": false}], \"E\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Hartley is 49% (outside 51-59%) and Dana is second at 11%, which is wrong.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Dana is credited with 220 lines (11%), which is at lea